  "number": 2695,
  "state": "closed",
  "locked": false,
  "title": "fix(session): reset empty-turn content without removing its message identity",
  "user": {
    "login": "yanyihan-xiaomi",
    "id": 209727656,
    "node_id": "U_kgDODIAwqA",
    "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/209727656?v=4",
    "gravatar_id": "",
    "url": "https://api.github.com/users/yanyihan-xiaomi",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/yanyihan-xiaomi",
    "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yanyihan-xiaomi/followers",
    "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yanyihan-xiaomi/following{/other_user}",
    "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yanyihan-xiaomi/gists{/gist_id}",
    "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yanyihan-xiaomi/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
    "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yanyihan-xiaomi/subscriptions",
    "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yanyihan-xiaomi/orgs",
    "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yanyihan-xiaomi/repos",
    "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yanyihan-xiaomi/events{/privacy}",
    "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yanyihan-xiaomi/received_events",
    "type": "User",
    "user_view_type": "public",
    "site_admin": false
  },
  "body": "## Problem\n\nDropping a think-only/empty step used to delete the assistant message and then rebuild a shell under the **same** message ID for the retry. `ctx.assistantMessage` is constructed once in `SessionProcessor.create` and `Effect.retry` wraps its stream, so the retried content always lands on the ID that was just deleted.\n\nOn the wire that sequence is byte-identical to a late frame of an already-deleted entity:\n\n```\nmessage.removed → message.updated → message.part.updated\n```\n\nConsumers that order by events cannot separate \"rebuild\" from \"stale frame\", so they keep dropping the rebuilt content. In MiMo Desktop the session-state center treats it as a late frame: the retried answer never appears, switching sessions does not help (history reads are gated by the same deletion fact), and only an engine restart recovers it.\n\nUser-visible symptom: occasionally one assistant reply disappears entirely while every other message is fine, recovered by restarting the engine. Frequency scales with how often the model emits think-only output, so it shows up rarely but across many users.\n\n## Change\n\nReset the content, keep the identity: remove the message's parts and leave the message in place, then reset `finish` / `error` / `time.completed` and hand back to `Effect.retry`.\n\nThis mirrors what the retry cleanup in the same file (`Effect.tapError`) already does — it removes parts and never touches the message identity. Parts are taken from the message-scoped `MessageV2.parts(...)` snapshot already read for classification, so every internal step is covered.\n\nContract unchanged: trigger condition, retry request history, and the final persisted shape (exactly one assistant message carrying the retried answer) are all untouched.\n\n## Not touched\n\n- The Desktop deletion tombstone stays as-is. It is correct: reads and events are two connections with no cross-connection ordering, so the tombstone is the only thing preventing a pre-query live event from resurrecting a pruned row.\n- Other `removeMessage` call sites (revert, compaction, resume trim, cleanupEmptyResidue, dropEmptyAssistant, REST delete) are genuine deletions and never rebuild under the same identity. `dropEmptyAssistant` in particular mints a fresh ID on the next step.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `bun run typecheck` (repo root) — PASS, all four workspaces clean.\n- `cd packages/cli && bun test test/session` — PASS, 1397 pass / 13 skip / 1 todo / 0 fail, 1411 tests across 125 files.\n- After the review follow-ups: `bun run typecheck` PASS, and `bun test test/session/invalid-output-continuation.test.ts test/session/retry.test.ts test/session/classify.test.ts` — PASS, 151 pass / 0 fail.\n- Regression is RED→GREEN. Before the change the new test failed with the final assistant's own ID present in the collected `message.removed` list; after the change no removal is published.\n\nIndependent review found no critical issues. Two pre-merge items (a stale comment describing the old delete-and-rebuild behaviour, and unrecorded verification in the spec) plus one inaccurate exhaustion claim were fixed and re-verified.\n\nFeature document: `docs/compose/spec/empty-turn-part-reset.md`.\n",
